<mujoco model="track_b_b3_two_body_contacts_enabled">
  <!--
    B3.4: Native collision, Track B (MuJoCo backend).

    Identical to b3_two_body_placeholder.xml (B3.1) in every respect
    except ONE flag: contact is "enable" here instead of "disable".
    B3.1's own file header already named this as the intended later
    path ("B3.4's own framing implies flipping this one flag back to
    enable"); this file is exactly that, not a redesign.

    WHY this is genuinely "essentially for free", confirmed directly
    against MuJoCo's own documentation (see conversation), not assumed:
    the full-override architecture's wrench injection
    (_inject_full_override_wrench in mujoco_backend.py) cancels and
    replaces ONLY qfrc_bias; MuJoCo's own documented "Coriolis,
    centrifugal and gravitational forces" term. Contact/constraint
    forces are a SEPARATE quantity entirely (qfrc_constraint, derived
    from efc_force via the constraint Jacobian); MuJoCo's own equation
    of motion adds bias and constraint forces separately, never combining
    them into one term. This means the override mechanism structurally
    CANNOT interfere with contact forces: it never touches them, by
    construction, regardless of whether contacts are enabled or
    disabled. Enabling this flag therefore does not require any change
    to mujoco_backend.py's own wrench-injection logic at all; contact
    forces simply appear as an additional, independent contribution to
    qacc whenever MuJoCo's own collision detection finds an active
    contact, layered on top of whatever the calibrated physics already
    supplies.

    Body 1 (auv_placeholder) and body 2 (auv_placeholder_2) are
    otherwise UNCHANGED from B3.1; same positions, same inertial
    properties, same geoms. At their default 2m separation, their boxes
    (each 0.3 x 0.15 x 0.15) never overlap, so this file alone does not
    by itself produce a contact. b3_4_native_collision_test.py
    deliberately moves them together to actually exercise collision
    detection, rather than relying on it happening to occur through
    ordinary motion.
  -->
  <option gravity="0 0 -9.81">
    <flag contact="enable"/>
  </option>

  <worldbody>
    <body name="auv_placeholder" pos="0 0 0">
      <freejoint/>
      <inertial pos="0 0 0" mass="11.2" diaginertia="0.15 0.25 0.20"/>
      <geom type="box" size="0.3 0.15 0.15" rgba="0.2 0.5 0.8 1"/>
    </body>

    <body name="auv_placeholder_2" pos="2 0 0">
      <freejoint/>
      <inertial pos="0 0 0" mass="11.2" diaginertia="0.15 0.25 0.20"/>
      <geom type="box" size="0.3 0.15 0.15" rgba="0.8 0.4 0.2 1"/>
    </body>
  </worldbody>
</mujoco>